+    identical defects landed on opposite sides of the line. Section 7.7's V
+    corrects the number with the harness's falsifier verdict but does nothing
+    about the asserted number's own noise while unresolved -- it halves the
+    band and the wobble travels with it. The ONLY operation that reduces that
+    noise without new machinery is repeated measurement, and the registry
+    ALREADY HOLDS the repeats: `record_codiscovery` is non-destructive (founder
+    ruling), so when k seats raise one defect, k canonicals each carry an
+    independently asserted severity -- and the current ruler reads exactly ONE
+    of them (whoever filed first) and discards the other k-1.
+
+    WHAT IS POOLED: the entry's own asserted severity plus the asserted
+    severity of every registration named by `from_canonical` in this entry's
+    codiscovery occasions -- the DIRECT star, each member individually
+    adjudicated as the same defect. NOT the transitive component that
+    `_corroborated_discounts` unions: measured on the 2026-10-15 third-leg
+    shakedown, transitive chaining links 20 of 38 canonicals into one component
+    with within-component spread 0.50 (severities 0.4..0.9, REFUTED and
+    CONFIRMED members mixed), while the direct stars of the same run stay
+    tight where corroboration is genuine (C0001: [0.9,0.9,0.85,0.9,0.85,0.78],
+    spread 0.12, consistent with the founder's 0.14 wobble). Transitivity was
+    never adjudicated; pooling across it would average distinct defects.
+
+    WHY THE MEDIAN: robust to one bad link or one outlier seat (archived stars
+    carry spreads up to 0.55). Noise arithmetic, normal noise sigma=0.14, SD of
+    the median of k = 0.14/0.099/0.094/0.077/0.075 at k=1/2/3/4/5 (exact
+    order-statistic constants 1, 0.7071, 0.6698, 0.5462, 0.5356 by quadrature;
+    k=3 and k=5 confirmed with Wolfram Language to 10 decimals). So k>=4 brings
+    the wobble BELOW the 0.09 half-band; k=2..3 reduce it without curing it;
